  "description": "Keep It Unreal is the second studio album by English disc jockey Andrew Carthy, under the alias Mr. Scruff. It includes the hit single \"Get a Move On!\", which is an electro swing track built upon samples of Moondog's \"Bird's Lament \" alongside vocals from T-Bone Walker's \"Hypin' Woman Blues\". The album ends with \"Fish\", a track made up of samples about marine life, which is a motif of Mr. Scruff. Samples used in the track include the likes of David Attenborough and David Bellamy. It was re-released in 2009 as a 10th anniversary two disc set.",
